Error [jet.ValueTypeMismatch]: `double` wants Int (a whole number) here, but this is String (text)
  --> main.jet:2:36
    |
  2 | first: fn() -> Int { helper.double("two") }
    |                                    ^^^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use Int (a whole number) here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0112

Error [jet.OperatorTypeMismatch]: Text isn't joined with `+`
  --> main.jet:3:33
    |
  3 | second: fn() -> String { helper.label(4) + 1 }
    |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: There's one way to build text: interpolation (S8)
 Fix: Write the pieces inside one interpolated string (schematic: the checked operands are not simple names)
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0109

Error [jet.UnknownFunction]: Nothing named `unknown_call` exists here
  --> main.jet:4:22
    |
  4 | third: fn() -> Int { unknown_call(3) }
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Only functions that have been defined (or built in, like `print` / `panic`) can be called
 Fix: Define it first (fn unknown_call() { ... }), or call one that exists
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0102

Error [jet.OperatorTypeMismatch]: `==` can't compare or combine Bool (true or false) and String (text)
  --> main.jet:5:31
    |
  5 | fourth: fn() -> Bool { helper.flag(2) == "yes" }
    |                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The operator has no built-in rule and no user-defined `impl Type.Trait` hook for this operand pair
 Fix: Use a supported operand pair, call a named method, or implement the operator's hook trait on your own type for this pair
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0109

Error [jet.ReturnTypeMismatch]: This value is Int (a whole number), but `label` returns String
  --> helper.jet:2:35
    |
  2 | label: fn(value: Int) -> String { value }
    |                                   ^^^^^
 Why: `label` declares String as its result, so the value it hands back must be String
 Fix: Put the value in text with interpolation: "{value}"
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0113

Error [jet.UnknownName]: Nothing named `missing` exists here
  --> helper.jet:3:60
    |
  3 | ratio: fn(total: Int, count: Int) -> Int { total / count + missing }
    |                                                            ^^^^^^^
 Why: A name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: Declare it first: `missing: ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

Error [jet.ReturnTypeMismatch]: This value is Int (a whole number), but `flag` returns Bool
  --> helper.jet:4:32
    |
  4 | flag: fn(value: Int) -> Bool { value + 1 }
    |                                ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `flag` declares Bool as its result, so the value it hands back must be Bool
 Fix: Hand back a Bool value: convert this value to Bool, or return the value you meant
